  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sint Maarten, one of the Constituent Countries of the Kingdom of the Netherlands, has been before the Committee on Application of Standards (CAS) since 2022 concerning the application of C87 on freedom of association. The case concerns representation of employers in Sint Maarten.

Beneficiaries of this initiative will include the government and employers, but also workers by achieving clear representation of the social partners at various fora. The ILO will provide technical and advisory services in collaboration with the Ministry of Public Health, Social Development and Labor, the social partners (especially the employers), and other relevant entities, such as the Social Economic Council (SER).</narrative>
  </description>
